preConditionHook:
// THE SESSION'S FIRST BAR IS A SMALL DOJI SITTING INSIDE YESTERDAY'S CLOSING
// RANGE -- a stronger trading-range-day bias than a doji open alone, because
// the market has opened with no information at all.
//
// Four terms: the session boundary, the doji body test, a SIZE test (the bar's
// range is no larger than dojiRangeFraction of the ATR, which is what "small"
// adds to "doji"), and containment inside the high-low block of the previous
// session's last closingRangeBars bars.
//
// IT DOES NOT LATCH. The merge pass recorded both readings as defensible and
// asked the authoring pass to pick one: this rule is the ONE-BAR filter and
// FirstBarOfSessionDoji is the latched twin, so the pair covers both without
// either being ambiguous. A placement that wants the latched form ANDs
// FirstBarOfSessionDoji instead.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: day_of(ctx.Time(0)) >
// day_of(ctx.Time(1)), the EasyLanguage twin's date > date[1] (EL_Date_Probe
// measured Date as the bar's wall-clock closing date on 169/169 bars). The
// comparison is on integer day serials, not prices, so it is exact and does
// not go through el_gt; the boolean lands in a local because a rule CONDITION
// may not carry a raw relational operator.
//
// THE CONTAINMENT BLOCK is Highest(high, closingRangeBars)[1] and
// Lowest(low, closingRangeBars)[1] -- the N bars ENDING ONE BAR AGO, so the
// first bar of the session is not in its own benchmark. On the session's first
// bar those N bars are the previous session's last N, which is exactly what
// the rule means by yesterday's closing range. Highest/Lowest bottom out in
// EL's Extremes(), EL SOURCE: seeded at the window's first bar, scanning the
// rest with a strict tolerance-carrying comparison, which is why the scan uses
// el_gt / el_lt and not raw > and <.
//
// closingRangeBars = 5 is a guess: Brooks gives no count.
//
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_AvgTrueRange is a ROLLING accumulator, not a fresh N-term
// sum: seeded with a full sum on the study's first calculated bar, thereafter
// carrying S += TrueRange - TrueRange[Length], re-seeding when the length
// changes. The update is TWO separate statements, as AtrProfitTarget writes it.
//
// Direction-agnostic -- it is a day-type bias, not a direction -- so both sides
// are identical text. Intraday bars only.
//
// Deepest bar touched: max(atrLookback + 1, closingRangeBars).
if (atrLenState != (int)atrLookback) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLookback; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrLenState = (int)atrLookback;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLookback;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atrValue = atrSum / (int)atrLookback;
priorHigh = high[1];
priorLow = low[1];
for (int i = 2; i <= (int)closingRangeBars; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], priorHigh)) priorHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], priorLow)) priorLow = low[i];
}
newSess = day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1));
